=== a backtick in a name
sql: SELECT "Album"."a`b" FROM "Album"
=== a double quote in a name
sql: SELECT "Album"."a""b" FROM "Album"
=== a name of 64 characters
sql: SELECT * FROM "éééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééé"
=== a name of 65 characters
sql: SELECT * FROM "ééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééééé"
=== a name of 128 bytes
sql: SELECT * FROM "nnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnn"
=== a name of 129 bytes
error: from: table name: identifier is 129 characters, over the engine limit of 128
=== a name of 64 characters outside the Basic Multilingual Plane
sql: SELECT * FROM "😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀😀"
=== a name of 65 characters outside the Basic Multilingual Plane
error: from: table name: identifier is 130 characters, over the engine limit of 128
=== a character outside the Basic Multilingual Plane
sql: SELECT "Album"."emoji😀" FROM "Album"
=== a name ending with a space
sql: SELECT "Album"."Title " FROM "Album"
=== an alias of 65 characters is declined
sql: SELECT "Album"."Title" AS "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" FROM "Album"
=== a table alias
sql: SELECT "a"."Title" FROM "Album" AS "a" WHERE "a"."AlbumId" = @p1
#1 int64 1
=== an output named as another column is no capture: every field is qualified
sql: SELECT "Album"."AlbumId" AS "Title", "Album"."Title" AS "AlbumId" FROM "Album" ORDER BY "Album"."AlbumId" ASC, ((CAST(("Album"."Title") AS FLOAT)) + (CAST(("Album"."ArtistId") AS FLOAT))) DESC
=== GROUP BY a column, HAVING an aggregate of a column an output is named after
sql: SELECT "Invoice"."BillingCountry" AS "Total", SUM(CAST(("Invoice"."Total") AS FLOAT)) AS "BillingCountry" FROM "Invoice" GROUP BY "Invoice"."BillingCountry" HAVING SUM(CAST(("Invoice"."Total") AS FLOAT)) > @p1
#1 int64 1
